--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY — web numeric pipeline ported VERBATIM (covenant #5)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Five RadialGauges in web render order (HeroGauges.Adapter.swift → HeroGaugesProjector):
  1 Distance    round(convertDistanceFromSI(distanceM, distance)); max(=*1.5,100); unit=distance; cyan  #00f0ff
  2 Max Speed   round(stats.maxSpd[display]);  max=convertSpeedFromSI(250, speed);  unit=speed;   purple#a855f7
  3 Duration    round((durationS ?? 0)/60);    max(=*1.5,60);      unit="min";                   amber #f59e0b
  4 Consumption round(toEffDisplay(consumptionWhKm)); max(=*1.5,300); unit=Wh/mi|Wh/km;           red   #ef4444
  5 Efficiency  Number(fmtNumber(efficiencyPctPer100)); max=30; unit=%/100mi|%/100km; — rendered ONLY
               when efficiencyPctPer100 != nil (web `{stats.efficiencyPctPer100 != null && …}`);   green #10b981
RadialGauge internals reproduced: clamped=max(0,min(v,max)); decimals = isInteger(clamped)?0:globalPrecision(2);
fraction=clamped/max. Constants NIST-exact: METERS_PER_MILE=1609.344, _KM=1000, _FOOT=0.3048; SECONDS_PER_HOUR
=3600; toEffDisplay = distance=='mi'? whPerKm*1.609344 : whPerKm. JS Math.round = floor(x+0.5). The
`Number(fmtNumber(x))` grouping→NaN quirk is mirrored (Double("1,234.50")=nil→NaN→safeNumber→0).
maxSpd is already display-unit (useDriveDetailData `toSpeedDisplay(maxSpeedMps)`) and consumed as-is, exactly
as the web does; the speed gauge's `convertSpeedFromSI(250,…)` max bound is ported verbatim (not "fixed").

